      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The Right to Repair movement is essential because it prevents manufacturers from creating artificial barriers that limit consumer choice and strain e-waste systems. When companies control spare parts and software, they effectively establish monopolies that inflate costs beyond what the market rate should dictate. By challenging these practices, activists ensure fair competition and force tech giants to innovate responsibly for all users rather than just locking them in specifically created ecosystems.",
