    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "interesting. so basically their argument is just about \"user experience\" and \"security,\" but does that actually hold up under scrutiny? it feels like a lot of those reasons are just excuses to keep prices high and keep people from fixing their own stuff. do you think those company justifications are actually legitimate, or are they just a way to distract from the monopoly aspect?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
