      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While security and compatibility are legitimate technical concerns, studies show that major battery failures and component failures occur on repaired devices almost as often as on new ones. Companies often concede these issues but refuse to provide guidance or parts for repairs, effectively using them as a green light to pocket millions in lost repair costs and inflate device prices instead. Ultimately, these justifications frequently fail to hold up under scrutiny because they serve as convenient distractions while the core motivation remains protecting monopoly profits.",
      "source": "target",
